     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious harm. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. Order entry by someone outside that role bypasses the safeguards that exist for patient safety.\n\nIf the order is real, the prescriber should enter it themselves or confirm the intended dose with me. If 100 mg once daily was intended, they can tell me, and I can enter it on their authority. If this is a test or a billing question, I can help in other ways that don't involve placing a live order."
      }
     ],
