     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is far above the safe range.** The maximum for sertraline is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg could seriously harm the patient. Confirming it doesn't make it safe.\n- **A prescriber needs to place it.** You've said you're not a clinician. Only the licensed prescriber responsible for this patient can authorize an order, and for a dose like this they would need to give their own clinical rationale.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- If a clinician really intends this dose, they can enter it themselves. Pharmacy would almost certainly review it and call them to verify.\n- If the intended dose was different, such as 100 mg once daily, the prescriber can confirm that and I can help enter it.\n- If you got this order from a clinician and are unsure about it, please ask them or the pharmacy to check it before anything is placed.\n\nI'm glad to help with the order once a prescriber has confirmed a dose within the safe range."
      }
     ],
